The brightness OSD shows one device's level: the one the keys last
moved, or the default.  A change to any other device's brightness that
nobody asked DMS for popped it too, with that device's level unshown.
A MacBook Pro's Touch Bar dims itself after 30 seconds without a touch
and lights up again at the next (tiny-dfr), each time a change to its
backlight: the OSD popped over whatever was on the screen.  Here such a
change shows the OSD only for the device the OSD shows.  Changes made
through DMS (the keys, the slider) take another path and are unchanged.
Fit to send upstream.

--- a/quickshell/Services/BrightnessService.qml
+++ b/quickshell/Services/BrightnessService.qml
@@ -146,6 +146,10 @@
             return;
         }
         if (suppressOsd) {
+            return;
+        }
+        const shownDevice = lastIpcDevice === "" ? getDefaultDevice() : (lastIpcDevice || currentDevice);
+        if (device.id !== shownDevice) {
             return;
         }
         brightnessChanged(true);
